ress and\n  heading) as depth shows it: at :summary its heading and its lead's first sentence, and how\n  much it left (:seon.ref/left, the sections below) with the citation that reads the rest\n  (:seon.ref/rest, its own address at :doc depth); at :doc its lead (or opening block) and the\n  sections below; at :code s whole. With no lead it answers :no-lead at :summary and :doc. One\n  rule for a section parsed now and a section the store holds.\"\n  {:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :seon.ref/view :seon.ref/depth] :seon.ref/view]}\n  [s depth]\n  (let [{:seon.ref/keys [lead opening below address]} s\n        head (select-keys s [:seon.ref/address :seon.ref/heading])]\n    (if (= :code depth)\n      s\n      (cond-> (case depth\n                :summary (cond-> (assoc head :seon.ref/left (count below)\n                                             :seon.ref/rest {:seon.ref/address address :seon.ref/depth :doc})\n                           lead (assoc :seon.ref/summary (lead-sentence lead)))\n                :doc (cond-> (assoc head :seon.ref/below (vec below))\n                       lead (assoc :seon.ref/lead lead)\n                       opening (assoc :seon.ref/opening opening)))\n        (nil? lead) (assoc :seon.ref/problem-kind :no-lead)))))\n(println (shown {:seon.ref/address \"docs/flow.md#flow\" :seon.ref/heading \"Flow\"\n                 :seon.ref/lead \"Flow runs procs, e.g. steps. More here.\"\n                 :seon.ref/below [{:seon.ref/address \"a\" :seon.ref/heading \"A\"}\n                                  {:seon.ref/address \"b\" :seon.ref/heading \"B\"}]}\n                :summary))" "(println (source seon.docs/view))\n(println \"----- citation attrs\")\n(->> (seon.db/entity (seon.agent/db) :seon.ref/citation) :seon.db/entity/attributes keys sort)" "(println (:seon.ref/text (my.agent/help \"docs/references.md#a-section-read-at-a-depth-with-its-edges\")))\n(println \"-----\")\n(println (my.agent/help \"docs/references.md#sections-in-a-tasks-context\"))" "(i